\title{#{\neg P}}
\date{2026-02-09T11:59:53Z}
\tag{discrete}
\tag{draft}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{Note that #{\neg P \equiv P \implies \False}.}

\p{Hence, to prove a proposition of the form #{\neg P}, prove #{P \implies \False}.}

\p{If you know #{\neg P}, then you know #{P \implies \False}.}
